WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:05.480
<b>In half an hour
 from now</b>

00:00.490 --> 00:03.370
In half an hour from now...

00:03.370 --> 00:05.020
...one of us dies.

00:03.370 --> 00:05.480
<b> one of us
 dies</b>

00:07.700 --> 00:08.930
Now...

00:09.130 --> 00:10.200
Now...

00:10.200 --> 00:13.020
Now, now, now!

00:13.020 --> 00:15.080
Time for a belated explanation!

00:15.800 --> 00:19.470
Until now, the two of you were 
imprisoned in the lowest level.

00:19.470 --> 00:22.570
A special ability space created 
to hold dangerous Gifted,

00:22.570 --> 00:25.710
known casually as the Happy Ball!

00:25.710 --> 00:29.790
Right now, we're a level above it, on the 
fourth floor of the general detention area.

00:29.790 --> 00:34.580
Still, the world's most elite security firms are 
standing watch on the route to the surface.

00:36.290 --> 00:41.150
First, the halls of each floor are 
divided into dozens of <i>cells</i>.

00:41.150 --> 00:45.780
A twelve-digit key is needed 
to pass through each.

00:45.780 --> 00:49.530
The keys are changed every six hours.

00:49.530 --> 00:53.810
Get it wrong once, 
and it'll never open again.

00:59.530 --> 01:04.030
The walls and doors of each cell are 
a whopping 120 centimeters thick!

01:04.030 --> 01:07.650
And they're made of anti-special ability metals,
making them impossible to break through.

01:09.650 --> 01:14.580
Even if you get through past the walls, 
the elevators are even more of a pain.

01:15.440 --> 01:19.320
The only way to get to the higher levels 
is aboard one of these elevators.

01:19.320 --> 01:23.570
But operating them requires
handprint, voiceprint, retina,

01:23.570 --> 01:26.660
as well as DNA identification.

01:26.660 --> 01:27.970
I hope you've had plenty to eat...

01:30.400 --> 01:32.480
Because there's still more!

01:32.480 --> 01:36.210
Heavily armed guards patrol each floor.

01:36.210 --> 01:38.670
They'll shoot on sight.

01:39.580 --> 01:41.100
Man!

01:41.100 --> 01:47.110
I love my plan, but neither of you are 
getting out even if you had a million lives.

01:47.500 --> 01:48.410
Oh!

01:48.950 --> 01:52.380
I forgot to tell you about the worst part.

01:52.380 --> 01:55.640
As soon as an intruder is detected,
 the blast doors close

01:55.640 --> 01:58.170
and the cells are filled with 
water ten seconds later.

02:00.620 --> 02:03.060
And just for good measure, 
it's not regular water,

02:03.060 --> 02:06.060
but heavy water, made from a 
different isotope of hydrogen.

02:06.060 --> 02:11.270
It's denser than normal water,
which makes it very difficult to swim in.

02:11.850 --> 02:16.160
It's also toxic, and will 
kill you if you drink enough.

02:16.790 --> 02:22.390
Of course, you'll die in thirty minutes 
from the poison we injected anyway.

02:22.760 --> 02:23.490
Well?

02:23.490 --> 02:25.170
Do you want to cry yet?

02:28.380 --> 02:29.730
<i>These guys...</i>

02:29.730 --> 02:33.350
<i>They're gleefully picturing 
the other drowning to death.</i>

02:33.780 --> 02:34.990
Now!

02:34.990 --> 02:37.420
I'll top it off with some good news!

02:37.420 --> 02:44.390
In honor of your march towards certain doom,
I've got a bit of a present for you!

02:45.780 --> 02:47.700
Assistant, bring me <i>the thing</i>.

02:47.700 --> 02:49.440
I'm not your assistant!

02:53.790 --> 02:57.890
I'll allow you each to 
take one of these items.

02:57.890 --> 03:01.030
They're powerful weapons that 
may lead to your victory.

03:01.360 --> 03:04.290
First, a radio used by the armed guards.

03:04.620 --> 03:07.530
You'll need one of these to 
know where the guards are.

03:08.130 --> 03:11.910
Second, a top level clearance door card.

03:12.260 --> 03:16.060
The door to the ocean heliport can 
only be opened with one of these.

03:16.490 --> 03:18.530
Third, coin bombs.

03:18.530 --> 03:19.930
Now with extra explosives!

03:20.200 --> 03:23.210
Leftovers from when I snuck in here.

03:23.570 --> 03:26.080
Fourth, a satellite phone.

03:26.080 --> 03:28.520
There's radio reception on the first floor.

03:28.520 --> 03:32.780
If you make it there, you can request help 
from any of your accomplices worldwide.

03:32.780 --> 03:34.890
In some ways, it's the most powerful weapon.

03:35.340 --> 03:37.640
<i>The question is which ones they'll choose.</i>

03:37.640 --> 03:39.120
I see.

03:39.520 --> 03:41.330
So the battle...

03:41.330 --> 03:44.020
has already begun.

03:45.120 --> 03:46.880
Feel free to choose first.

03:47.670 --> 03:50.400
Why, thank you very much.

03:51.630 --> 03:53.750
I'll take this one.

03:54.280 --> 03:55.720
I see!

03:55.720 --> 03:57.290
Very well.

03:57.580 --> 04:00.970
<i>That door card is needed 
to make it to the exit.</i>

04:00.970 --> 04:03.340
<i>It's absolutely necessary to win.</i>

04:03.750 --> 04:07.390
<i>Fyodor's actions are 
incomprehensible and freakish,</i>

04:07.920 --> 04:11.510
<i>but in fact, he's more calculating 
and rational than anyone.</i>

04:11.760 --> 04:15.240
Now, Dazai-kun, what will you choose?

04:18.070 --> 04:19.560
Let's see...

04:19.560 --> 04:21.910
I like this one.

04:26.230 --> 04:27.160
Me?!

04:29.890 --> 04:31.640
I like you!

04:31.640 --> 04:32.620
You're great.

04:33.350 --> 04:35.090
<i>What are you...</i>

04:35.540 --> 04:37.020
<i>...thinking?</i>

06:06.630 --> 06:09.640
<b>Episode 57 
At the Port in the Sky 
(Part 3)</b>

06:11.120 --> 06:13.900
It's just like Dad said a long time ago.

06:13.900 --> 06:19.230
Airport exits are made to be easy 
to secure for security reasons.

06:19.760 --> 06:21.070
Your dad?

06:21.070 --> 06:23.340
My dad's a cop.

06:24.070 --> 06:27.340
No, never mind him.

06:28.300 --> 06:33.670
The point is, it's really hard to get out 
of an airport once it's locked down.

06:34.150 --> 06:35.530
Just to be sure...

06:35.530 --> 06:38.240
You can't give those guards 
orders, can you, Bra-chan?

06:38.240 --> 06:39.660
It's impossible.

06:39.660 --> 06:43.000
My powers have been taken 
away by this holy sword.

06:43.540 --> 06:48.680
The only time I can command my kin 
is when Fukuchi wields the sword.

06:48.680 --> 06:50.180
Seriously?

06:50.770 --> 06:52.100
What do we do?

06:52.710 --> 06:54.610
Do you have any ideas?

06:54.610 --> 06:55.510
I do.

06:56.150 --> 06:58.750
Dig a hole and sleep for 
two hundred years or so.

06:58.750 --> 07:00.570
Wait for the situation to improve.

07:00.860 --> 07:04.960
You'd be a total slouch if it weren't 
for your ability, wouldn't you?

07:04.960 --> 07:09.400
Girl, are you a fast runner?

07:09.770 --> 07:12.810
I'm the fastest sprinter in my class. Why?

07:13.310 --> 07:14.780
That's most fortunate.

07:15.160 --> 07:15.750
Run!

07:22.040 --> 07:23.440
Answer my question!

07:23.440 --> 07:25.010
Why me?

07:25.370 --> 07:28.050
Why did you choose me from all those things?

07:28.050 --> 07:29.160
What are you plotting?

07:29.500 --> 07:33.320
Do you know what I'm thinking right now?

07:33.320 --> 07:33.930
What?

07:34.270 --> 07:35.630
It's so big!

07:35.630 --> 07:39.950
Compared to living in that cramped cell,
it's like a ballroom!

07:39.950 --> 07:41.270
Let's dance!

07:42.990 --> 07:45.400
What are you going to use me for?

07:45.400 --> 07:47.080
How will you defeat Fyodor?

07:47.660 --> 07:48.610
Also...

07:48.610 --> 07:49.600
Stop!

07:52.940 --> 07:54.330
I stopped.

07:54.940 --> 07:56.200
You...

07:56.200 --> 07:57.940
Stop dicking around for once!

07:58.470 --> 08:01.500
Fyodor's getting closer 
to the exit as we speak!

08:01.880 --> 08:04.200
I'm not sure about that.

08:05.180 --> 08:06.700
Aren't you going?

08:07.040 --> 08:09.600
It's been five minutes 
since the game started.

08:09.600 --> 08:13.570
You can still swap your little present 
for another one if you want.

08:14.120 --> 08:17.000
I have another card to play.

08:17.350 --> 08:18.530
I see.

08:19.280 --> 08:22.430
You've got your own tricks up your sleeves.

08:33.520 --> 08:34.910
Disrespectful.

08:37.570 --> 08:39.090
Thanks, Bra-chan!

08:41.890 --> 08:43.070
Oh, no!

08:44.190 --> 08:45.420
We're surrounded!

08:45.940 --> 08:47.210
Escape on your own.

08:47.520 --> 08:49.970
I'm the only one they're after.

08:49.970 --> 08:50.720
I can't.

08:50.720 --> 08:51.470
Not that.

08:51.860 --> 08:54.300
If they take you, it's all over.

08:58.210 --> 08:59.540
<i>What do I do?</i>

09:00.070 --> 09:01.660
<i>What am I supposed to do?</i>

09:02.320 --> 09:04.320
You're a failure of a woman!

09:06.550 --> 09:07.990
<i>What do I...</i>

09:09.090 --> 09:11.020
This is what you do!

09:20.220 --> 09:22.610
Rampo-san told me to come help you.

09:24.940 --> 09:27.890
Oh, so fun!

09:27.890 --> 09:30.510
How wonderful freedom is!

09:31.910 --> 09:34.040
Come on. How long are you going to dance?

09:34.380 --> 09:36.330
Don't forget about the game!

09:38.440 --> 09:40.780
Wanna go tour around the jail?

09:40.780 --> 09:43.420
It's not somewhere you 
get to see all the time!

09:43.420 --> 09:45.560
You might as well go tour hell!

09:45.910 --> 09:47.300
Oh, I know!

09:49.750 --> 09:51.390
Hey, where are you going?

09:51.390 --> 09:53.270
The exit isn't that way.

09:53.270 --> 09:55.480
I'm going to the staff pantry.

09:55.480 --> 09:57.230
I got so bored of prison food.

09:57.230 --> 09:59.030
I want a bellyfull of sweet stuff!

10:00.870 --> 10:02.780
I'm leaving on my own.

10:04.980 --> 10:07.390
You have no chance against Fyodor.

10:07.390 --> 10:08.760
That's clear to me now.

10:10.390 --> 10:13.510
I can't allow myself to lose.

10:13.500 --> 10:17.220
<b><i><b>Five days ago—</b></i></b>

10:14.420 --> 10:17.220
Expose Fyodor's ability?

10:17.690 --> 10:20.220
I'm grateful that you saved me,

10:20.760 --> 10:23.130
but there's no way I could 
accomplish something like that.

10:23.490 --> 10:25.470
Why me, anyway?

10:25.710 --> 10:27.830
Because I think it'd be fun.

10:27.830 --> 10:30.500
<i>Right, that's the kind of person he is.</i>

10:31.110 --> 10:33.810
Though, this request is 
to your benefit, too.

10:34.820 --> 10:39.260
Fyodor-kun will find out soon enough 
that your assassination was a failure.

10:39.260 --> 10:44.340
In other words, unless you kill him, 
you'll never find a peaceful home.

10:46.740 --> 10:47.620
Home?

10:49.130 --> 10:53.600
<i>It shocked me how strongly 
that word spoke to me.</i>

10:54.500 --> 10:57.770
<i>Everyone in the world has a 
home that they're born to.</i>

10:58.460 --> 10:59.940
<i>Except me.</i>

11:01.190 --> 11:06.590
<i>I was born from nothing, and someone 
has been manipulating me ever since.</i>

11:07.210 --> 11:08.300
<i>Fyodor.</i>

11:09.030 --> 11:10.150
<i>Nikolai.</i>

11:10.460 --> 11:12.780
<i>And Dazai.</i>

11:18.580 --> 11:20.680
<i>I'm defeating Fyodor.</i>

11:20.680 --> 11:24.860
<i>And I'm going to find my own home, 
where I can be safe from others.</i>

11:26.140 --> 11:28.950
<i>I won't let anyone use me anymore.</i>

11:31.270 --> 11:32.620
I see how it is.

11:33.100 --> 11:35.010
You're lotsa fun!

11:35.330 --> 11:36.380
Okay!

11:36.380 --> 11:39.370
I promise I'll get you out of here alive.

11:39.370 --> 11:40.770
Get off me!

11:44.370 --> 11:45.570
What was that?

11:45.570 --> 11:46.720
Was that from a higher floor?

11:53.790 --> 11:57.270
Have you heard of the most powerful 
Gifted guard in this prison?

11:57.930 --> 12:01.490
Briareus, the Hundred-Hander?

12:01.920 --> 12:05.620
You're looking at him right now.

12:06.310 --> 12:11.150
I'm impressed, intruder.

12:12.520 --> 12:14.030
It's quiet again.

12:14.290 --> 12:15.900
It's an intruder.

12:17.960 --> 12:18.780
How do you know?

12:20.730 --> 12:23.020
An angel whispered so in my ear.

12:23.020 --> 12:24.570
An angel?

12:24.570 --> 12:25.940
What are you talking about?

12:27.540 --> 12:29.130
<i>Some kind of communicator?</i>

12:29.660 --> 12:31.850
<i>He doesn't have a radio, though.</i>

12:32.930 --> 12:35.530
And who is this intruder?

12:35.530 --> 12:37.910
Who else would it be?

12:38.300 --> 12:40.180
One of Fyodor's men?

12:48.120 --> 12:49.690
Whoa, holy shit!

12:49.690 --> 12:51.830
Well, time to bounce!

12:57.090 --> 12:59.660
Prisoner D18, don't move!

12:59.660 --> 13:00.900
Raise your hands.

13:00.900 --> 13:02.670
Resist, and you will be shot.

13:10.210 --> 13:12.720
I finally have my pawns.

13:17.910 --> 13:19.550
Wow...

13:19.550 --> 13:21.310
I see.

13:21.310 --> 13:23.860
I know who the intruder is now.

13:25.690 --> 13:27.490
<i>Intruder on Level 4!</i>

13:27.490 --> 13:28.520
<i>Backup—</i>

13:28.860 --> 13:30.460
Damn it, Fyodor...

13:30.460 --> 13:32.820
That's one nasty card he's playing.

13:34.440 --> 13:36.040
<i>This Gifted intruder...</i>

13:36.040 --> 13:39.990
...manipulates gravity!

13:39.990 --> 13:42.550
It's Nakahara Chuuya!

13:46.590 --> 13:48.340
Nakahara Chuuya?

13:48.790 --> 13:52.360
That makes it two-versus-two.

13:52.360 --> 13:56.480
It's me and you against Fyodor and Chuuya.

13:57.000 --> 13:59.460
<i>W-We don't stand a chance.</i>

14:03.440 --> 14:08.740
<b>Do you know the phrase "tear away and toss"?</b>

14:03.740 --> 14:08.400
<i>Do you know the phrase "tear away and toss"?</i>

14:08.730 --> 14:12.380
<i>I've always thought it was a weird phrase.</i>

14:12.380 --> 14:17.040
<i>I mean, what kind of situation 
is that, tearing and tossing?</i>

14:17.040 --> 14:19.080
<i>But I get it now.</i>

14:25.020 --> 14:27.650
<i></i>This<i> is what it means.</i>

14:29.210 --> 14:30.430
There.

14:31.350 --> 14:32.840
All clean.

14:33.140 --> 14:34.460
Um...

14:34.460 --> 14:37.020
You're the guy from the 
Detective Agency, aren't you?

14:37.020 --> 14:38.440
Why are you here?

14:38.440 --> 14:40.860
I'm following Rampo-san's 
instructions, of course.

14:41.760 --> 14:43.310
A sudden airport lockdown.

14:43.670 --> 14:46.230
The vampires looking for someone.

14:46.230 --> 14:50.110
An abandoned coffin and 
countless katana marks.

14:50.370 --> 14:56.830
It wasn't hard for Rampo-san to figure out 
that someone's running from Fukuchi.

14:57.070 --> 15:03.820
Anyway, my job is to rescue you 
and deliver you to safety.

15:03.820 --> 15:06.830
I'll take you to a safe 
special ability space.

15:07.230 --> 15:08.770
Well, let's go!

15:08.770 --> 15:09.650
Hold it.

15:09.650 --> 15:11.670
That outfit...

15:12.030 --> 15:13.350
It smells of dirt.

15:13.750 --> 15:14.910
Are you a farmer?

15:15.950 --> 15:18.650
Are you interested in cultivating my land?

15:19.060 --> 15:21.160
Is this really the time to be head-hunting?

15:21.160 --> 15:23.340
You probably don't even have any land.

15:23.720 --> 15:25.340
Thank you!

15:26.190 --> 15:28.930
But I'm already working on my own farm,

15:28.930 --> 15:32.280
and I'm a member of the 
Detective Agency on the side.

15:32.780 --> 15:33.950
It's a side gig?

15:36.390 --> 15:40.810
Say, mister decapitated head, 
do you get wolves on your land?

15:40.810 --> 15:42.230
Wolves?

15:42.230 --> 15:43.920
Ah, I do.

15:43.920 --> 15:47.590
Pesky beats that attack my sheep.

15:48.410 --> 15:51.100
You must understand the 
current situation, then.

15:51.610 --> 15:53.220
There's a wolf here now.

16:05.180 --> 16:07.330
Evil begone.

16:07.630 --> 16:10.190
I have to protect the sheep.

16:10.630 --> 16:12.280
<i>Hurry! Hurry!</i>

16:12.280 --> 16:15.530
<i>Rampo-san said the rules of 
the battle have changed.</i>

16:17.130 --> 16:23.430
This isn't so much close-quarters guerrilla 
warfare anymore as it is a ball game.

16:23.910 --> 16:28.830
Whoever chases Bram and the 
girl onto their own turf wins.

16:29.580 --> 16:32.510
Do you know what that means, Atsushi?

16:32.830 --> 16:35.310
It means that you, 
the fastest runner, are the key.

16:42.390 --> 16:43.810
<i>That girl...</i>

16:44.420 --> 16:45.690
<i>Is that...?</i>

16:45.990 --> 16:46.840
What's wrong?

16:46.840 --> 16:47.870
Are you all right?

16:48.300 --> 16:50.680
I was separated from 
someone important to me.

16:51.550 --> 16:52.900
But it's okay.

16:52.900 --> 16:54.350
I finally found them.

16:54.350 --> 16:55.290
Oh.

16:55.290 --> 16:56.440
That's good, then.

16:56.800 --> 16:58.960
But who's this important person?

16:58.960 --> 17:00.500
You.

17:04.100 --> 17:07.880
Exciting, isn't it? 
My beloved wanted criminal!

17:08.230 --> 17:10.740
I can't wait to hear how you scream.

17:11.290 --> 17:12.620
<i>A Hunting Dog!</i>

17:14.660 --> 17:16.750
Guy from the Detective Agency!

17:16.750 --> 17:18.080
Run away without me.

17:18.390 --> 17:21.090
I'm not sure if I can beat him or not.

17:23.060 --> 17:24.770
Let's go, Bra-chan!

17:24.770 --> 17:26.290
What about the security?

17:26.290 --> 17:27.390
It's fine.

17:27.390 --> 17:28.910
I have an idea.

17:29.450 --> 17:31.020
Die not, peasant!

17:31.020 --> 17:33.880
Thank you for your patience.

17:33.880 --> 17:35.000
Of course.

17:35.490 --> 17:38.780
It's you I have business with, 
Detective Agency.

17:38.780 --> 17:39.730
Me?

17:40.160 --> 17:41.400
Where's Jouno?

17:43.680 --> 17:45.820
Jouno's missing.

17:45.820 --> 17:46.910
What have you done with him?

17:47.200 --> 17:50.340
You're looking for someone named Jouno-san?

17:50.340 --> 17:51.360
That's right.

17:51.360 --> 17:52.570
Where is he?

17:52.570 --> 17:53.590
I don't know.

17:53.940 --> 17:55.470
Shall I help you look for him?

17:56.130 --> 17:57.050
What?

17:57.050 --> 17:58.840
You're gonna help me find him?

17:59.210 --> 18:00.090
Yup!

18:00.090 --> 18:01.350
That'd be great.

18:04.530 --> 18:05.510
No, wait.

18:06.330 --> 18:07.970
Sorry, I made a mistake.

18:08.880 --> 18:13.740
I'm told that Jouno was captured by the 
vampires when he was with the Captain.

18:14.690 --> 18:16.760
In other words,
 the Detective Agency is behind it.

18:18.360 --> 18:20.480
I really don't know, though.

18:20.810 --> 18:24.440
Then why did you let the 
leader of the vampires go?

18:24.780 --> 18:27.410
Ah, there's a reason for that.

18:31.670 --> 18:34.300
I apologize, but I don't have time to chat.

18:34.570 --> 18:36.320
I'm helping Jouno.

18:36.320 --> 18:39.120
And I'm doing that in the 
quickest way possible.

18:46.150 --> 18:49.860
Now, then, what shall
 I have you tell me first?

18:49.860 --> 18:52.320
How about we start with your will?

18:52.320 --> 18:55.530
I keep killing people before 
I get to hear them.

18:55.530 --> 18:58.240
<i>She won't budge,
even with my tiger strength.</i>

19:01.240 --> 19:02.040
Oops.

19:04.540 --> 19:07.540
Were you about to contact your buddies?

19:07.540 --> 19:08.950
What a waste of effort.

19:10.430 --> 19:12.340
Not quite.

19:12.980 --> 19:16.300
<i>Teruko-san, if you're watching this,</i>

19:16.300 --> 19:20.390
<i>it means that I'm dead or 
enduring something even worse.</i>

19:20.390 --> 19:21.720
Tachihara...

19:22.880 --> 19:24.700
You said you were looking for me?

19:25.170 --> 19:26.150
You're wrong.

19:26.490 --> 19:28.150
I was looking for <i>you</i>.

19:28.980 --> 19:31.050
So I could show you that.

19:31.340 --> 19:33.290
<i>I won't pretend I'm okay with this.</i>

19:33.750 --> 19:37.300
<i>Just thinking about being 
dead makes me sick.</i>

19:37.780 --> 19:41.280
<i>But it'd be even worse dying in vain,</i>

19:41.830 --> 19:43.840
<i>so I'll report on my investigation.</i>

19:44.960 --> 19:46.910
<i>The Detective Agency was innocent.</i>

19:50.450 --> 19:52.430
A falsified video.

19:52.430 --> 19:55.000
Think what you want, then.

19:55.680 --> 19:56.870
<i>I'm going, now.</i>

19:57.500 --> 20:04.660
<i>Honestly, I'm really not the type to 
risk my life on some damn mission.</i>

20:05.760 --> 20:09.650
<i>Maybe I'm finally a little closer 
to being an exhilarating badass.</i>

20:12.700 --> 20:13.970
Tachihara...

20:14.540 --> 20:19.410
The heroes of justice are gonna 
go save the world wounded.

20:19.410 --> 20:22.650
Don't you think this makes for 
quite the exhilarating picture?

20:23.150 --> 20:24.240
<i>Well, then...</i>

20:25.360 --> 20:27.800
He's been missing since then.

20:28.240 --> 20:29.970
The enemy mastermind probably got him.

20:31.730 --> 20:32.940
So?

20:32.940 --> 20:34.640
What's the Detective Agency's plan?

20:35.390 --> 20:37.370
If you'll cooperate, I'll tell you.

20:37.900 --> 20:39.260
On one condition.

20:39.570 --> 20:42.190
I want to meet the person 
proposing the Agency's plans.

20:42.800 --> 20:44.150
Rampo-san?

20:44.480 --> 20:48.340
Showing me this video was part 
of his plan, too, wasn't it?

20:48.340 --> 20:50.550
How cocky.

20:50.830 --> 20:54.270
I'll decide whether or not to 
help after I meet with him.

20:54.510 --> 20:57.040
<i>That's definitely too dangerous.</i>

20:57.580 --> 21:03.450
<i>There's no guarantee she's overcome the page
 and trusts the Detective Agency like Tachihara.</i>

21:04.550 --> 21:08.400
<i>But if she does, we can get 
the Hunting Dogs on our side.</i>

21:10.080 --> 21:11.260
All right.

21:11.690 --> 21:13.200
Give me a moment.

21:16.800 --> 21:20.250
<i>Rampo-san would have a 
chance at convincing her.</i>

21:47.530 --> 21:50.200
Is this the Detective Agency's 
brute-force Gifted?

21:50.790 --> 21:52.620
He's fierce.

21:52.620 --> 21:53.460
But...

21:56.220 --> 21:57.780
<i>He's so strong!</i>

21:58.130 --> 22:00.800
I am a Hunting Dog!

23:36.020 --> 23:40.010
Next Episode
Episode 58

23:36.020 --> 23:40.010
<i>Land of Inhuman Demons (Part 1)</i>
